<title>USA: MAPCO seen issuing $200 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>MAPCO seen issuing $200 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>MAPCO Inc is expected to issue $200 million in a two-tranche debt deal on Friday, according to market sources.</p>
<p>The first tranche is expected to consist of $100 million in 12-year notes, with price talk in the 73 basis point area.</p>
<p>The second tranche is expected to consist of $100 million in 30-year debentures, with price talk in the 85 basis point area.</p>
<p>Both tranches are non-callable and are rated Baa2 by Moody's Investors Service and BBB by Standard and Poor's.</p>
<p>((- Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
